Package: gamlssPosthoc
Type: Package
Title: Marginal and Distributional Post-Hoc Inference for GAMLSS Models
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person(given = c("Walter", "Esfrain"), family = "Pereira",
    email = "walterufpb@yahoo.com.br", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1085-0191"))
Description: Provides a conservative post-hoc workflow for generalized additive
    models for location, scale and shape (GAMLSS), primarily fitted with the
    'gamlss' package. The package routes simple
    parameter-wise comparisons to 'emmeans' when supported and uses
    standardized predictions, full predictive distributions, and refit
    bootstrap procedures for smoothers, derived estimands, zero-adjusted
    models, trends, and custom functions of multiple distributional
    parameters. The framework follows the distributional-regression principles
    of Rigby and Stasinopoulos (2005) <doi:10.1111/j.1467-9876.2005.00510.x>.
    The emphasis is on stable inference for means, contrasts, polynomial
    trends, and distribution-derived quantities in applied experiments.
